            <ArticleTitle>4-arylphthalazin-1(2H)-one derivatives as potent antagonists of the melanin concentrating hormone receptor 1 (MCH-R1).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>427-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2011.10.111</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel series of 4-arylphthalazin-1(2H)-one linked to arylpiperidines were synthesized and evaluated as MCH-R1 antagonists. The results of an extensive SAR study probing the effects of substituents on the 4-arylphthalazin-1(2H)-one C-4 aryl group led to the identification of the 4-(3,4-difluorophenyl) derivative as a highly potent MCH-R1 inhibitor with an IC(50)=1nM. However, further investigations showed that this substance has unacceptable pharmacokinetic properties including a high clearance and volume of distribution.</AbstractText>
